From e73c1e42c556b100180893eea9bbe510cf4bb7d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:00:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] glm cuda: kept prompt states spill into pinned host
 memory, and carry DFlash2's context to their mark

The prompt cache's pages had one tier: the device memory left after the streams, a GiB or less at
4 streams x 472K. Each rank now also pins a host tier (cuda_snapshot_host): TF_GLM_HOST_CACHE_GIB over
all ranks (0: off), or unset a quarter of MemAvailable at startup, at most 16 GiB in all. A state takes
free device pages first and host pages for the rest (one lease, two id lists); copies to and from the
host run on the engine stream from page-locked memory, so a restore stays a byte copy.

The ranks agree on the tier at the snapshots step: each reads its own MemAvailable, the least wins, and
if any rank fails to pin it every rank frees its tier and takes device pages alone. The store's budget
is the device cache plus the tier (native cuda_snaps cacheBudget's snap_host_tier).

A state beside DFlash2 also keeps the drafter's context ring when the pass tapped the rows right up to
its mark (dflash Slot.first/end), and a resume drafts from those rows as a fresh pass would, instead of
from the mark. TF_GLM_SNAP_DRAFTER=0 keeps the old behaviour (A/B).

Rank 0 logs each copy that touches host pages with its size and time.

